{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966803,"nonce":"rp8chogg9jwV/heB48uqiVaE4hc=","title":"A stateful subscribed to context fields that are only BOUND PROPS re-renders the whole","message":"**Symptom.** ~1s lag between clicking an FSM action button and the bound props\nupdating, while a different action felt instant. After a window resize the lag\nvanished (caches warm), which makes it look like a paint bug rather than a\nrender-count bug.\n\n**Cause (fixed 52ec34a4).** `3d91959c` had put EVERY context field of the bound\nFSM into the DSL root stateful's deps. The playground's `Grow` writes five\nfields, all of them bound to props (`Progress(value)`, `Skeleton(w/h/rounded)`,\n`Separator(opacity)`) -- work the property channel already does in place. Each\nwrite notified the stateful, so one click re-rendered the whole program five\ntimes. Compounded by the DSL mounting ONE stateful at the view root\n(project dsl scoped stateful), so \"re-render\" means everything.\n\n**The rule.** Mentioning a context field has two meanings, and only one needs a\nre-render:\n\n    Play.pct          binding handle -\u003e property channel writes in place\n    Play.busy.get()   value read     -\u003e only a re-render can follow it\n\nDeps are the value reads: branch conditions, interpolations, anything a repaint\ncannot express. A bare `X.y` in an argument position is a handle and is\nexcluded. `computed { … }` bodies are skipped, since the prop binds to the\nderived, not to the fields inside it.\n\n**Measured, one dispatch on the playground:**\n\n    Grow  5 re-renders + 78ms rebuild  -\u003e  0 re-renders, 125ns\n    Busy  1 re-render                  -\u003e  1  (writes busy AND caption;\n                                              only busy is read as a value)\n\n**Reproduction:** `crates/blinc_cn_dsl/tests/pg_grow_cost.rs`. Counts the\n\"stateful container: on_state re-render\" debug line with a `tracing_subscriber`\nLayer, so the assertion is on RENDER COUNT, not on wall-clock. Both directions\nare asserted: Grow must be 0, Busy must be exactly 1. Install\n`set_stateful_deps_notifier` or nothing fires at all.\n\n**Debugging note.** The user's own `RUST_LOG=debug` output showed five\n`on_state re-render` lines ~6ms apart for one click. That log line is the\ncheapest instrument for this class of bug -- reach for it before theorising\nabout repaint scheduling.\n\nSee feedback signal subtree not full tree, feedback stateful is rebuild hatch,\nproject dsl scoped stateful.","files":null}]}